## What NOT to Do
- Never violate SOLID principles
- Never use deep inheritance hierarchies
- Never use `any` in TypeScript (use `unknown`)
- Never use `enum` in TypeScript (use `as const`)
- Never discard errors silently in Go
- Never use Lombok `@Data` in Java (use Records)
